# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SA–Türkiye Sovereign AI & Digital Trade Sandbox — environment template
# Copy to .env.local (development) or configure in Vercel → Settings → Env Vars
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SQLite (Phase 1 sandbox). Phase 2 swaps to a managed PostgreSQL URL.
DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"

# ── Information Integrity Engine — signing credentials (OPTIONAL) ────────────
# Leave unset to use the embedded sandbox demo keypair (clearly marked as
# demo material). For production, provide a base64 PKCS#8 Ed25519 private key
# and a base64 SPKI public key — generated, for example, with:
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm ed25519 | openssl pkey -outform DER | base64 -w0
#   openssl pkey -in private.pem -pubout -outform DER | base64 -w0
# In Phase 2 these are replaced by HSM/KMS custody with a documented key
# ceremony; the env-var path exists for pre-HSM staging deployments.
# SANDBOX_PRIVATE_KEY=""
# SANDBOX_PUBLIC_KEY=""

# ── AI inference pipeline (REQUIRED on Vercel for policy analysis) ───────────
# The sandbox runtime ships with /etc/.z-ai-config. On Vercel, set both vars;
# the SDK bootstraps its config into a writable temp home automatically.
# ZAI_API_KEY=""
# ZAI_BASE_URL=""
